---
import PageHeader from "@components/PageHeader.astro";
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Impossible Safe"
  description="A safe cracking game for iPhone inspired by a Apple Watch game."
>
  <PageHeader title="The Impossible Safe" />

  <img
    src="/images/the-impossible-safe-cover.webp"
    alt="The Impossible Safe"
    width="720"
    height="360"
    class="mb-10 w-full rounded-xl"
  />

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      A few years ago I saw Rafael Conde's <a
        href="http://breakthissafe.com/"
        title="Break This Safe"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">Break This Safe</a
      >, but when I got to try it for myself it didn't seem to work as intended.
      Maybe a couple WatchOS releases broke something vital for the game.
    </p>
    <p>
      However the concept stuck in my head and when I created my first iPhone
      App, The Box Timer, I tought that "hey, this is probably something I can
      pull off".
    </p>
    <p>
      With my newfound confidence I spent a couple of weekends hacking away,
      trying to build something that was both fun and simple enought for me to
      actually complete.
    </p>
    <p>
      The result is the game you see today – enjoy it as much as I did creating
      it!
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-10 flex justify-center">
    <a
      href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/the-impossible-safe/id1573468310"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
      title="The Impossible Safe on the App Store"
    >
      <img
        src="/images/appstore-badge.svg"
        alt="Download The Impossible Safe on the App Store"
        width="250"
        height="54"
      />
    </a>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
